        "math_academy_id": "q-349147",
        "problem": "Evaluate the following integral of a vector-valued function. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{4}\u27e8{t}^{2}-2t,\\,3{t}^{3}+t\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t=\u27e8$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $\u27e9$",
        "worked_solution": "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\u27e8{t}^{2}-2t,\\,3{t}^{3}+t\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & =\u27e8{\\int }_{0}^{4}({t}^{2}-2t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{4}(3{t}^{3}+t)\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first component,\n\n$$\n\\int ({t}^{2}-2t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFor the second component,\n\n$$\n\\int (3{t}^{3}+t)\\,\\text{d}t=3\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{t}^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\u27e8{t}^{2}-2t,\\,3{t}^{3}+t\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & =\u27e8(\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{4},\\,(\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{4}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8(\\frac{1}{3}(64)-16)-0,\\,(\\frac{3}{4}(256)+\\frac{1}{2}(16))-0\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8(\\frac{64}{3}-16),\\,(192+8)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{16}{3},\\,200\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{16}{3},\\,200\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
